A fragment has much more corpus frequency in longer words than as a whole
word. Negative estimates are strongest after subject or auxiliary cues.
A count of English function words chooses English versus multilingual
frequencies. Capitalization and dictionary verb readings grade the response;
Chinese verb glosses provide a smaller cue. Document starts are separate.
This captures a limited facet, not a complete parser or token-value table.
